## Installation Instructions

```bash
git clone <this-repo>
cd hospital-patient-flow-analysis
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## How to Run the Notebook

```bash
jupyter notebook notebooks/hospital_patient_flow_analysis.ipynb
# Run all cells — fixed random seed reproduces the exact same dataset and results,
# and regenerates data/raw/, data/processed/, and visuals/charts/
```

## How to Run the SQL Analysis

```bash
cd sql
python build_database.py
sqlite3 hospital_patient_flow.db < queries/01_volume_and_trends.sql
# or open hospital_patient_flow.db in DB Browser for SQLite / any SQLite client
```

## How to Reproduce the Dataset

The dataset is generated entirely within Section 1 of the notebook using `np.random.seed(42)` — running the notebook end-to-end regenerates byte-for-byte the same raw and cleaned datasets referenced throughout this README.

## Disclaimer

**All data, patients, timestamps, and findings in this project are synthetic and generated for educational and portfolio purposes.** "Chilungamo District Hospital" is a fictional institution. Nothing in this repository represents real patients, real hospital operations, or real Ministry of Health data, and no figures here should be interpreted as describing any actual healthcare facility in Malawi or elsewhere.

## Portfolio Positioning

Demonstrates: SQL (JOINs, CTEs, window functions) · Python/Pandas · data cleaning and data-quality investigation · statistical analysis (non-parametric testing, chosen deliberately for the data's actual distribution) · healthcare and operational analytics · data visualization · Power BI dashboard design · business/management reporting · problem-solving (including a documented, real bug found and fixed in the SQL layer). Machine learning is deliberately not the focus of this project — see Project 2 for a modest, explainable classifier, and later portfolio projects for a deeper ML focus.

